  // ConnectionStrings live in this file on purpose (accepted exception, audit finding
  // dotnet.production-connection-strings-not-keyvault, 2026-09-21). Every entry authenticates
  // with "Active Directory Default" — the App Service's managed identity — so the strings hold
  // only a server host and database name, never a credential. Key Vault's @Microsoft.KeyVault
  // reference pattern exists to keep secrets out of config; there is no secret here to keep out,
  // and moving hostnames behind a vault lookup would add a runtime dependency without protecting
  // anything. Revisit only if a connection string ever needs a password or key.
